# `core.autocrlf=true` on this checkout rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which
# breaks every shell launcher on the Linux runner: bash reads the first real
# statement as `set -Eeuo pipefail\r` and exits 2 with
# `set: pipefail: invalid option name` before any of the script's own validation.
# Forcing LF for shell scripts makes the working tree match what actually runs.
# tests/test_shell_line_endings.py checks the raw bytes as a second line of defence.
*.sh text eol=lf
